My 10th(!) level Valkyrie (86 HP, -3 AC, +3 longsword) ran into some
demons (Hezrou?) on level 5(!) when going upstairs to finish up some
unfinished levels.  They kicked my butt while continuing to gate in more
of their demon friends.  Well, needless to say I didn't wait around to
play with them.

To make a long story even longer, I came back after I picked up a pet
Balrog (polyorph trap) who took care of all of the demons except for one
he wouldn't touch -- Jubilex!!  After a few of his/its engulfments and my
running out of teleport devices I was down to 10 HP.  I stumbled across
"Elbereth" I had engraved on the floor when I first crossed the level
(there was a sink in the room...) and put on my ring of levitation.

Jubilex would teleport in, I would hit him a couple of times, then he
would teleport back out to regenerate.  I looked in my pack and found two
very useful potions: paralysis and sickness.  When he teleported in next,
I threw the paralysis potion at him, then the sickness potion.  This had
the effect of keeping him from teleporting away and/or attacking me while
also cutting his HP in half.  After a few swipes with my sword, Jubilex
was done.

I have never run into a major demon that early in a game (either dungeon
level or character level), and was lucky to live through that one.  A
little unfair I must say, although that would have been *some* bones level
-- imagine running into a Balrog AND Jubilex on level 5!  No one could
have gotten past that.  Maybe a chaotic.

Another answer to your question is to get to the stairs before the demon
and stand on them, that way he will just stand next to you and take the
punishment.  Also, the paralysis/sickness one-two punch works well against
most any tough opponent -- truly devastating.

